Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 20:05:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: FeedHomeButton wasn't self-explanatory - replaced
 ambiguous Unicode icon with a real SVG house icon plus an always-visible
 'Home' label
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Confirmed the actual problem: every single usage across the app (all
5 dashboards + car detail page) used the icon-only variant, and the
icon itself was '⌂' - a Unicode character, not a proper icon, easy to
miss or misread as decoration rather than a button. No place in the
app ever showed the 'labeled' variant that did exist.

Rebuilt as one component with a clear house-shaped SVG icon and a
'Home' text label always shown, not hidden behind hover or a
tooltip - this is now what renders everywhere automatically, no
caller changes needed since none passed any props. Label only hides
on genuinely tiny screens (360px and below) to avoid topbar overflow,
kept at a narrow breakpoint specifically so it stays visible on the
vast majority of real devices rather than defeating the whole point
of the fix.
