From efcbf41e257a09985a72a5563a4c312387d13496 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 04:48:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: replace fake background removal with real AI
 segmentation - it genuinely wasn't removing anything before

Root cause confirmed: the previous implementation only detected and
made transparent pixels close to pure white - it was honest about
this in its own code comments, but that meant it did literally
nothing for any photo with a real background (a car photo, a logo on
a colored background, a signature photographed on a desk) - exactly
matching the 'not removing anything' complaint.

Replaced with @imgly/background-removal - a real neural-network-based
subject segmentation model (ONNX via WebAssembly), the same category
of technology behind remove.bg and most 'perfect' background removal
tools. Runs entirely client-side - no server cost, no API key,
nothing ever leaves the device, keeping the app's existing zero-cost,
privacy-preserving approach for this feature.

Researched and confirmed before integrating: the exact required
onnxruntime-web peer dependency version (an unusual dev-build version
string, verified consistently across three independent official
sources rather than guessed), and checked the app's own next.config.js
for any Content-Security-Policy restrictions that could block WASM
compilation in production (a real, documented failure mode for this
exact library elsewhere) - confirmed none exist here, so that risk
doesn't apply to this app.

Kept the old near-white method as an automatic fallback
(removeBackgroundSmart) rather than removing it outright - if the AI
model can't load (offline on first use, restrictive network), the
person still gets a working result instead of a hard failure, with a
clear notice explaining what happened and that retrying may give a
better result. Also lazy-loaded via dynamic import so the ~40-80MB
model files are never part of the app's normal page-load bundle -
they only download when someone actually uses this feature.

BackgroundRemovalPreview.tsx updated to show live progress during
processing (model download / removal progress) instead of a bare
spinner, and the hint text no longer claims this only works on white
backgrounds, since that's no longer true.
